    "title": "Quasi symmetric plane partitions enumeration conjecture",
    "statement": "Let $\\operatorname{qspp}(a,c)$ denote the number of quasi symmetric plane partitions inside an $(a,a,c)$-box. Let $p_a(c)$ be a polynomial in $\\mathbb{Q}[c]$. **Quasi symmetric plane partitions conjecture.**\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{qspp}(a,c-a)=\\begin{cases}\nc\\binom{c+a-1}{2a-1}p_a(c)&a\\text{ is even},\\\\\n\\binom{c+a-1}{2a-1}p_a(c)&a\\text{ is odd},\n\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nHere $p_a(c)$ is irreducible and even, meaning $p_a(c)=p_a(-c)$, and the common denominator of its coefficients is a product of “small primes”. This is one of three conjectural enumeration formulas obtained from computer experiments; the claimed formulas are supported by data for small parameter values.",
